---
title: Ploceidae
---
# Ploceidae

Ploceidae is the weaver family of Africa and southern Asia, about a hundred and
twenty species of small, thick-billed, mostly seed-eating songbirds. The male of
most species plaits a roofed chamber from strips torn out of palm or reed
leaves, knotting and twining each strip against the last around the tip of a
slender branch. The finished chamber is slung below the branch and entered from
underneath, which puts it out of reach of a snake working along the limb. A
female inspects several chambers and tugs at the structure; a poorly plaited one
is abandoned and the male dismantles it. See [[village-weaver]].
